          "path": "_m/g/c/d/1/roscommon-wp/thomas-charles-macdermotroe-of.jpg",
          "filename": "Thomas Charles MacDermotRoe of Alderford, Cty Roscommon, Ireland.jpg",
          "caption": "Thomas Charles MacDermot Roe, 1847-1913, was the Anglo Irish chieftain of the MacDermot Roe family from 1855-1913. He served as High Sheriff of County Roscommon and Justice of the Peace of the Counties Roscommon and Sligo.  He was succeeded by his brother Ffrench Fitzgerald MacDermot Roe. Since neither had male heirs, the line went extinct in 1917.",
